A palette is loaded again when TEX1 names another bank at the draw

A palette is loaded at the TEX0 write, from the block that TEX0's CBP and the
bank of the TEX1 before it name together (patch 0006). A writer that sets
TEX1 after TEX0 (the sampling last) therefore loaded the palette from the
bank of the texture before: the right low bits in the wrong bank.

The interface now remembers, for each context, the palette bank (TEX1's
CBP_BANK) at the context's last TEX0 write. A textured draw of a context
whose TEX1 names another bank by then loads the palette again first, exactly
as that TEX0 write would have with the bank in place (handle_clut_upload: the
CLD rule, the cached pointers), and remembers the new bank. The usual order,
TEX1 then TEX0, is untouched: the bank at the draw is the bank at the TEX0
write.

The remembered banks are state beside the registers: a caller that saves and
restores the registers around speculative drawing saves and restores them
(get_clut_load_banks, set_clut_load_banks), and a caller that replaces the
registers whole calls sync_clut_load_banks.

For a block below 16384 the bank is always zero and nothing is loaded again.

set_clut_bank_reload(false) is a control for tests: the palette stays the one
TEX0 loaded.

The lines are kept apart from those of the earlier patches, so that each
patch still reverse-checks on its own.

diff --git a/gs/gs_interface.cpp b/gs/gs_interface.cpp
index 5f8a1d8..a9a53dc 100644
--- a/gs/gs_interface.cpp
+++ b/gs/gs_interface.cpp
@@ -870,8 +870,41 @@ void GSInterface::handle_clut_upload(uint32_t ctx_index)
 	}
 }
 
+void GSInterface::get_clut_load_banks(uint32_t banks[2]) const
+{
+	banks[0] = clut_load_bank[0];
+	banks[1] = clut_load_bank[1];
+}
+
+void GSInterface::set_clut_load_banks(const uint32_t banks[2])
+{
+	clut_load_bank[0] = banks[0];
+	clut_load_bank[1] = banks[1];
+}
+
+void GSInterface::sync_clut_load_banks()
+{
+	clut_load_bank[0] = registers.ctx[0].tex1.desc.CBP_BANK;
+	clut_load_bank[1] = registers.ctx[1].tex1.desc.CBP_BANK;
+}
+
+void GSInterface::set_clut_bank_reload(bool enable)
+{
+	clut_bank_reload = enable;
+}
+
+// A textured draw of a context whose TEX1 names another palette bank than at its last TEX0 write: the palette is
+// loaded again, as that TEX0 write would have loaded it with the bank in place (the CLD rule, the cached pointers).
+void GSInterface::handle_clut_bank_change(uint32_t ctx_index)
+{
+	clut_load_bank[ctx_index] = registers.ctx[ctx_index].tex1.desc.CBP_BANK;
+	if (clut_bank_reload)
+		handle_clut_upload(ctx_index);
+}
+
 void GSInterface::handle_tex0_write(uint32_t ctx_index)
 {
+	clut_load_bank[ctx_index] = registers.ctx[ctx_index].tex1.desc.CBP_BANK;
 	handle_clut_upload(ctx_index);
 	tracker.flush_if_memory_pressure();
 }
@@ -2977,6 +3010,9 @@ void GSInterface::drawing_kick_primitive(bool adc)
 
 	if (!adc)
 	{
+		const uint32_t ctx_index = registers.prim.desc.CTXT;
+		if (registers.prim.desc.TME && uint32_t(registers.ctx[ctx_index].tex1.desc.CBP_BANK) != clut_load_bank[ctx_index])
+			handle_clut_bank_change(ctx_index);
 		if (!draw_is_degenerate())
 			drawing_kick_append<list_primitive, fan_primitive, quad, num_vertices>();
 		else
diff --git a/gs/gs_interface.hpp b/gs/gs_interface.hpp
index 64ff119..0ca28e1 100644
--- a/gs/gs_interface.hpp
+++ b/gs/gs_interface.hpp
@@ -673,6 +673,23 @@ private:
 	void reset_context_state_registers();
 
 	enum { MaxPromotedBackbuffers = 4 };
+public:
+	// The bank of each context's palette pointer (TEX1's CBP_BANK) at its last TEX0 write: the bank its palette was
+	// loaded from. A textured draw of a context whose TEX1 names another bank by then loads the palette again first,
+	// as that TEX0 write would have with the bank in place (a writer that sets TEX1 after TEX0). A caller that saves
+	// and restores the registers around speculative drawing saves and restores these with them; a caller that
+	// replaces the registers whole calls sync_clut_load_banks(): nothing is loaded again until a bank changes.
+	void get_clut_load_banks(uint32_t banks[2]) const;
+	void set_clut_load_banks(const uint32_t banks[2]);
+	void sync_clut_load_banks();
+	// false: the palette stays the one TEX0 loaded (a control for tests).
+	void set_clut_bank_reload(bool enable);
+
+private:
+	uint32_t clut_load_bank[2] = {};
+	bool clut_bank_reload = true;
+	void handle_clut_bank_change(uint32_t ctx_index);
+
 	PromotedBackbuffer promoted_backbuffers[MaxPromotedBackbuffers];
 	uint32_t num_promoted_backbuffers = 0;
 	void promote_render_pass_to_backbuffer(const RenderPass &rp);
